{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790460978,"nonce":"boVnZDG1Z01hVMZLM5vreRNQf9w=","message":"Decided with the user (2026-09-26): plugins support both modes, linked into the program and loaded as a side module, chosen per plugin by the build. Shared: plugin! exports every member under its caribou::link symbol (computed by a proc macro in caribou_abi_derive; the rule's naming function moves into caribou_abi so the macro and the core share it). The plugin's registry names give the symbol: lang = plugin name, module and class = the class name (a free function's class is the plugin name capitalised), kind t/c/m, arity without the receiver. Linked mode: the driver builds the plugin with --cfg caribou_static. The generic caribou_plugin_entry/caribou_abi_version then give way to per-plugin names, and plugin! emits caribou_plugin_link_\u003cname\u003e(), which registers the entry with the runtime (caribou_plugin_register, defined by caribou-runtime, referenced only in the static build). Ash's AotRequest gains init_calls, symbols called from ash_module_init, listing each linked plugin's link function. Call sites are direct. Side-module mode is ce0bba4.","files":null}]}